; worlddelete.eval — deleting a world (W9), GitHub's way: type the name.
;
; The confirmation's Delete stays disabled until the typed name matches EXACTLY,
; case and all. `worlds dialog confirm <text>` types into that field and presses
; the button, so a wrong name here is a press that must do nothing — and the
; `worlds` listing after each one is the evidence, read off disk.
;
; Leftovers are removed by WorldTest's cleanup, not here.
logecho on
reset
worldmap on
worlds new wt_del
worlds dialog
; The running world is refused before any confirmation opens.
worlds dialog delete dungeon-demo
worlds dialog delete wt_del
; Wrong case, then a prefix: both refused, the world still on disk after each.
worlds dialog confirm WT_DEL
worlds
worlds dialog confirm wt_de
worlds
; The exact name.
worlds dialog confirm wt_del
worlds
worlds dialog off
; The console's form: the name twice, exactly.
worlds new wt_del2
worlds delete wt_del2 WT_DEL2
worlds delete wt_del2 wt_del2
worlds
worlds delete wt_del2 wt_del2
